      "source": "source/SI-A_Sailing_Instructions_General_2026_v2.pdf",
      "url": "https://dbsc.ie/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/SI-A_Sailing_Instructions_General_2026_v2.pdf",
      "title": "AIB DBSC Summer Series 2026 sailing instructions A, general",
      "why": "A4.3 is what puts a course card in use: flag X ashore on a Saturday sends every keelboat class but the Green fleet to the West Pier hut, under supplement H and Course Card 2. A10.4 restricts passing between the hut and the start limit marks."
    },
    {
      "output": "source/SI-B_Sailing_Instructions_Fixed_Marks_Committee_Vessel_2026_v1.md",
      "source": "source/SI-B_Sailing_Instructions_Fixed_Marks_Committee_Vessel_2026_v1.pdf",
      "url": "https://dbsc.ie/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/SI-B_Sailing_Instructions_Fixed_Marks_Committee_Vessel_2026_v1.pdf",
      "title": "AIB DBSC Summer Series 2026 sailing instructions B, fixed-mark courses, committee vessel",
      "why": "B4.2 defines the committee vessel starting line that cards 1, 3 and 4 start at; B5.5 says which of them is used on which day; B5.6 gives the red/green “p”/“s” sides the cards print; B6 the finish."
    },
    {
      "output": "source/SI-H_Sailing_Instructions_Fixed_Marks_Hut_2026_v2.md",
      "source": "source/SI-H_Sailing_Instructions_Fixed_Marks_Hut_2026_v2.pdf",
      "url": "https://dbsc.ie/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/SI-H_Sailing_Instructions_Fixed_Marks_Hut_2026_v2.pdf",
      "title": "AIB DBSC Summer Series 2026 sailing instructions H, fixed-mark courses, hut",
      "why": "H4.1 and H4.2 define the West Pier hut starting line that cards 2 and 5 start at — a fixed transit, not a laid line — and H4.3 the limit mark; H5.5 says which card is used on which day; H5.6 makes Turning mark X a passing mark; H6.1 the finish, also at the hut."
    },
    {
      "output": "source/Sailing_Instructions_2026_Amendment2_CV_starts.md",
      "source": "source/Sailing_Instructions_2026_Amendment2_CV_starts.pdf",
      "url": "https://dbsc.ie/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Sailing_Instructions_2026_Amendment2_CV_starts.pdf",
      "title": "AIB DBSC Summer Series 2026 sailing instructions amendment 2, all committee vessel courses",
      "why": "Adds B4.3: if the committee vessel cannot anchor, the starting line may be between two marks, or a mark and a RIB. It is an alternative to B4.2, not a replacement, so the card’s start line quotes B4.2."
    },
    {
      "output": "source/Sailing_Instructions_2026_Amendment4.md",
      "source": "source/Sailing_Instructions_2026_Amendment4.pdf",
      "url": "https://dbsc.ie/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Sailing_Instructions_2026_Amendment4.pdf",
      "title": "AIB DBSC Summer Series 2026 sailing instructions amendment 4, Saturdays 29 August and 12 September",
      "why": "Adds B5.12: on those two Saturdays the Red Fleet and Dublin Bay 21s race Course Card 4 from Corinthian, and a course may be repeated (2A3) or two combined (A3B8). The card holds the courses as printed; combining them is the reader’s to do."
    }
  ],
